# Read by GitHub ("Cite this repository") and by Zenodo when a release is archived.
# Copied to the site root by scripts/supplementary/build.py -- edit it here, not in _site/.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these figures or their data, please cite them using the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: >-
  Supplementary material (interactive figures) for the PhD thesis "Efficient High Speed Modulation
  Techniques for a Sensing Application"
abstract: >-
  Interactive versions of figures from a PhD thesis on multiplexed
  time-of-flight secondary ion mass spectrometry (MP-ToF-SIMS) at The University
  of Manchester, with the reduced data each one draws. The thesis PDF is the
  examined record and carries a static version of every figure. Each page states
  whether its data are measured or illustrative, and records the source file,
  its SHA-256 and the code that reduced it.
authors:
  - family-names: Newman
    given-names: Mathew P.
    affiliation: The University of Manchester
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1784-3250
license: CC-BY-4.0   # pages and data; bundled Plotly (MIT) and IBM Plex (OFL-1.1) keep their own licences
keywords:
  - time-of-flight secondary ion mass spectrometry
  - ToF-SIMS
  - multiplexing
  - maximum-length sequences
  - Bradbury-Nielsen gate
  - ion beam modulation
  - interactive figures
repository-code: https://github.com/Thenewmanator15/mptofsims-supplementary
url: https://thenewmanator15.github.io/mptofsims-supplementary/
